From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:50:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] Windows: InvalidationTracker works in 16 KiB host
 protection units

A single Darwin write fault releases the whole 16 KiB backing page, so the fault
path invalidates that whole unit, and ProtectRWXIntervalsInternal re-arms and
invalidates every tracked RWX subpage sharing the host protection unit.

Source: MacRunner lane debug-teb-self-load/small-write-fex (navisworks, 11.09.2026);
exact file archived into libCommonWindows.a of MacRunner 1.0.2.

Portions derived from FEX-Emu, Copyright (c) 2019 Ryan Houdek and FEX contributors, MIT License.
Co-Authored-By: GPT-6 Astra <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
index 155403d35..4cf473dfc 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <FEXCore/Config/Config.h>
 #include <FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h>
 #include "InvalidationTracker.h"
+#include "MacRunnerHostPageGeometry.h"
 #include <windef.h>
 #include <winternl.h>
 
@@ -230,7 +231,8 @@ bool InvalidationTracker::HandleRWXAccessViolation(FEXCore::Core::InternalThread
     {
       std::scoped_lock Lock(CTX.GetCodeInvalidationMutex());
 
-      InvalidateIntervalInternalLocked(FaultAddress & FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_MASK, FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE);
+      // A single Darwin fault releases writes for the entire backing page.
+      InvalidateIntervalInternalLocked(FaultAddress & ProtectionPageMask, ProtectionPageSize);
 
       // Invalidate, then unprotect the faulting page with the compilation lock held to ensure that any racing invalidations are not dropped.
       ULONG TmpProt;
@@ -339,7 +341,11 @@ void InvalidationTracker::InvalidateIntervalInternalLocked(uint64_t Address, uin
 }
 
 bool InvalidationTracker::ProtectRWXIntervalsInternal(uint64_t Address, uint64_t Size, bool ForWriteLocked) {
-  const auto End = Address + Size;
+  if (!Size) return false;
+  // Re-arm all tracked RWX subpages sharing a host protection unit.
+  const auto End = (Address + Size + ProtectionPageSize - 1) & ProtectionPageMask;
+  const auto AlignedBase = Address & ProtectionPageMask;
+  Address = AlignedBase;
   std::shared_lock Lock(IntervalsLock);
 
   if (SMCDetectionDisabled) {
@@ -356,7 +362,8 @@ bool InvalidationTracker::ProtectRWXIntervalsInternal(uint64_t Address, uint64_t
           // applied and the invalidation mutex must be locked throughout.
           // Do this lazily only when an RWX region is actually hit.
           // NOTE: This assumes CodeInvalidationMutex is locked by the caller
-          InvalidateIntervalInternalLocked(Address, Size);
+          // Unprotecting releases the entire host-page range, not only the caller bytes.
+          InvalidateIntervalInternalLocked(AlignedBase, End - AlignedBase);
         }
         HitRWXInterval = true;
       }
